sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch02-14> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Phenomena not already known to exist can be found only by very systematic and general experiments whose results are examined with as few preconceptions as possible.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Unknown phenomena are found only by systematic, preconception-free experiments";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 2, “The Crucial Experiment”; section “Why These Discoveries Were Not Made Before” (from p. 42), p. 45. Scope: scientific methodology, especially computer experiments"
}
